---------------------------- MODULE EventcountTrace ---------------------------
(***************************************************************************)
(* Trace validation, as SchedDonationTrace's: the states of seeded runs    *)
(* of the Rust, crates/kipc's eventcount module, projected onto the        *)
(* spec's record, must start at Init and move only by the spec's steps.    *)
(* EventcountTraces is generated by the eventcount_traces test.  A step    *)
(* that isn't one of Next's leaves TraceNext disabled, so TLC, checking    *)
(* for deadlock, reports it.  The ASSUME rejects traces that don't start   *)
(* at Init, which TLC would pass as a model with no initial state.         *)
(***************************************************************************)
EXTENDS Eventcount, EventcountTraces, Sequences

ASSUME /\ Len(Traces) > 0
       /\ \A j \in 1..Len(Traces) : Len(Traces[j]) > 0 /\ Traces[j][1] = InitState

VARIABLES k, i

TraceInit ==
    /\ k \in 1..Len(Traces)
    /\ i = 1
    /\ s = Traces[k][1]
    /\ s = InitState

\* Next comes first, so it gives s' its value, and the trace's state is
\* then compared with that.  In the other order TLC v1.7.4 compares the
\* trace's tuples with the spec's functions, and can find an equal pair
\* unequal (a tuple against a function the spec built with EXCEPT), so a
\* valid step would deadlock.
TraceNext ==
    \/ /\ i < Len(Traces[k])
       /\ i' = i + 1
       /\ UNCHANGED k
       /\ (Next \/ UNCHANGED s)
       /\ s' = Traces[k][i + 1]
    \/ /\ i = Len(Traces[k])
       /\ UNCHANGED <<s, k, i>>

TraceSpec == TraceInit /\ [][TraceNext]_<<s, k, i>>

=============================================================================
